1
00:00:05,390 --> 00:00:06,230
There we go...

2
00:00:07,500 --> 00:00:09,900
I normally shut myself in at home,

3
00:00:10,370 --> 00:00:13,150
but unusually for me,
today I made up my mind to go out.

4
00:00:17,200 --> 00:00:19,620
All to get my hands on
the first-run limited edition

5
00:00:19,620 --> 00:00:22,510
of a popular online game
that goes on sale today.

6
00:00:31,130 --> 00:00:34,380
A five-hour round trip!
I'm glad I was able to buy it.

7
00:00:34,560 --> 00:00:38,110
In-store exclusives, official or not,
really are playing dirty.

8
00:00:40,970 --> 00:00:44,230
This sunlight is my worst enemy
after three straight all-nighters.

9
00:00:44,840 --> 00:00:46,980
Time to get home and play the hell out of this.

10
00:00:52,760 --> 00:00:54,270
A girl from my high school?

11
00:00:58,950 --> 00:01:01,450
Look out! That truck's going to—

12
00:01:05,930 --> 00:01:08,070
Why would I choose now, of all times,

13
00:01:08,070 --> 00:01:10,120
to do something so out of character?

14
00:01:24,910 --> 00:01:26,460
Satou Kazuma-san.

15
00:01:27,250 --> 00:01:29,110
Welcome to the afterlife.

16
00:01:31,970 --> 00:01:35,770
Unfortunately, you passed away moments ago.

17
00:01:39,800 --> 00:01:41,870
Your life was a short one,

18
00:01:43,730 --> 00:01:46,080
but you are, in fact, dead.

19
00:01:49,030 --> 00:01:50,040
Just one question...

20
00:01:52,060 --> 00:01:54,630
What about the girl I
pushed out of harm's way?

21
00:01:56,040 --> 00:01:57,350
She's alive.

22
00:01:59,850 --> 00:02:01,260
Thank goodness.

23
00:02:01,760 --> 00:02:04,350
That means my death wasn't in vain.

24
00:02:06,550 --> 00:02:08,770
Actually, she wouldn't have gotten hurt,

25
00:02:09,220 --> 00:02:11,600
even if you hadn't pushed her out of the way.

26
00:02:11,810 --> 00:02:12,610
Huh?

27
00:02:12,940 --> 00:02:16,610
That tractor was going to stop before it hit her.

28
00:02:16,610 --> 00:02:18,450
Huh? Wait a second.

29
00:02:18,450 --> 00:02:19,490
What is it?

30
00:02:19,760 --> 00:02:21,120
"Tractor"?

31
00:02:21,750 --> 00:02:24,000
Yes, it was a tractor.

32
00:02:24,450 --> 00:02:25,890
Huh? Then what happened?

33
00:02:26,270 --> 00:02:28,870
Did I die by getting plowed over by a tractor?

34
00:02:28,870 --> 00:02:30,920
No, you died of shock.

35
00:02:30,920 --> 00:02:33,130
You mistakenly thought a truck ran over you.

36
00:02:33,130 --> 00:02:34,290
I died of shock?!

37
00:02:38,610 --> 00:02:40,800
I've been doing this for a long time,

38
00:02:40,800 --> 00:02:44,350
but you're the first human to
ever die in such a bizarre way.

39
00:02:45,260 --> 00:02:48,730
I've never even met this girl
before. What's her deal?

40
00:02:48,730 --> 00:02:51,890
You were so terrified that you'd
be run over, you wet yourself.

41
00:02:51,890 --> 00:02:54,090
You passed out and were
taken to a nearby hospital,

42
00:02:54,090 --> 00:02:56,710
and the doctors and nurses laughed
at you as you had a heart attack—

43
00:02:56,710 --> 00:02:58,570
Stop! I don't wanna hear it!

44
00:02:58,570 --> 00:03:00,280
I don't wanna hear it! I don't wanna hear it!

45
00:03:00,280 --> 00:03:02,740
Your family just rushed to the hospital,

46
00:03:02,740 --> 00:03:05,590
and now even they're laughing
out loud at the cause of death.

47
00:03:05,590 --> 00:03:06,870
Stop! Stop!

48
00:03:06,870 --> 00:03:07,800
Well...

49
00:03:09,370 --> 00:03:12,120
I've vented enough stress for now.

50
00:03:12,670 --> 00:03:13,630
Damn her!

51
00:03:13,960 --> 00:03:15,600
My name is Aqua.

52
00:03:16,120 --> 00:03:19,840
I'm a goddess who guides humans
who die young to the afterlife.

53
00:03:20,130 --> 00:03:22,790
You have two choices.

54
00:03:23,250 --> 00:03:25,750
You can start from square one with a new life,

55
00:03:25,750 --> 00:03:29,430
or you can go to Heaven and
carry on like an old man.

56
00:03:29,760 --> 00:03:31,730
To tell you the truth,

57
00:03:32,220 --> 00:03:35,400
Heaven isn't the dreamy place
you all imagine it to be.

58
00:03:35,400 --> 00:03:36,120
Huh?

59
00:03:36,340 --> 00:03:38,780
Not only is there no TV, there are
no manga or games, either.

60
00:03:38,780 --> 00:03:40,530
You don't even have a physical body,

61
00:03:40,900 --> 00:03:44,080
so you can't do anything sexual, either.

62
00:03:44,520 --> 00:03:47,900
There's nothing to do there but
bask in the sun for all eternity.

63
00:03:47,900 --> 00:03:49,080
What?

64
00:03:49,570 --> 00:03:53,520
Yeah, you don't want to go to a
boring place like Heaven, do you?

65
00:03:53,520 --> 00:03:55,260
Uh, right...

66
00:03:55,510 --> 00:03:59,090
On the other hand, starting over
from square one isn't so fun, either.

67
00:03:59,090 --> 00:04:01,380
On that note, I've got a great offer for you.

68
00:04:01,570 --> 00:04:03,900
You like games, don't you?

69
00:04:03,900 --> 00:04:04,650
Huh?

70
00:04:05,330 --> 00:04:08,520
That world, which has long enjoyed peace,

71
00:04:08,520 --> 00:04:11,310
is being threatened by the Devil King's army!

72
00:04:11,580 --> 00:04:15,520
The livelihoods its citizens have worked
for are being trampled by monsters.

73
00:04:15,520 --> 00:04:20,320
Everyone lives in fear of the Devil King's
army's merciless pillage and slaughter!

74
00:04:20,950 --> 00:04:22,440
...slaughter!

75
00:04:24,970 --> 00:04:28,520
Since that's the sort of world it is,
everyone refuses to be reborn,

76
00:04:28,520 --> 00:04:30,120
so the population is declining.

77
00:04:30,320 --> 00:04:31,400
I see...

78
00:04:31,400 --> 00:04:33,900
So we decided, "Why not send people who've

79
00:04:33,900 --> 00:04:38,460
died in other worlds there with their
bodies and memories intact?"

80
00:04:38,960 --> 00:04:41,780
What's the point in sending me there
if I'm just going to be killed?

81
00:04:41,780 --> 00:04:43,440
That's why I'm doing you a big favor.

82
00:04:43,990 --> 00:04:47,940
I'm granting you the right to bring any
one thing of your choosing with you.

83
00:04:47,940 --> 00:04:51,180
It could be a powerful weapon,
or a tremendous talent.

84
00:04:51,390 --> 00:04:54,940
You'll be able to redo your life
with all of your original memories.

85
00:04:54,940 --> 00:04:57,770
To top it off, you can bring
one thing of your choosing!

86
00:04:58,150 --> 00:04:59,710
And the people of the parallel world

87
00:04:59,710 --> 00:05:01,920
will earn someone battle-ready to help them.

88
00:05:02,480 --> 00:05:04,460
Not a bad deal, don't you think?

89
00:05:07,930 --> 00:05:09,830
Um, I want to ask something.

90
00:05:10,330 --> 00:05:12,500
Will I be able to speak this
other world's language?

91
00:05:13,070 --> 00:05:14,830
That won't be an issue.

92
00:05:14,830 --> 00:05:16,210
Parallel World Reincarnation Guide and Contract
The First Ever Parallel World Guide! (For Shut-ins)

93
00:05:16,420 --> 00:05:19,080
With the kind support of us gods,

94
00:05:19,380 --> 00:05:23,290
we'll overload your brain so you'll
be able to learn it instantly.

95
00:05:22,550 --> 00:05:25,360
Caution!
Because the process of installing the ability to speak the parallel world's language into the one
who wishes to be reincarnated there (henceforth referred to as "Reincarnated") requires
instantaneous overloading of the hippocampus and cerebral cortex (henceforth referred to as
"Brain"), Reincarnated's Brain may, in rare cases, lose certain faculties (go "p**f"). Should
this occur, according to Article 1296 Clauses 2 and 5 and Article 2051 Clause 3,
Reincarnated may not hold those responsible for his reincarnation accountable.

96
00:05:23,290 --> 00:05:24,360
As a side effect,

97
00:05:24,360 --> 00:05:26,810
you might just go "poof"
if you're unlucky, though.

98
00:05:26,810 --> 00:05:30,330
So all that leaves you to do is to choose
a powerful ability or piece of equipment.

99
00:05:33,040 --> 00:05:35,760
I just heard you mention
something really serious.

100
00:05:36,540 --> 00:05:37,900
What do you mean, "poof"?

101
00:05:37,900 --> 00:05:38,980
I never said that.

102
00:05:38,980 --> 00:05:39,900
Yes, you did.

103
00:05:40,630 --> 00:05:42,460
Now, choose!

104
00:05:43,090 --> 00:05:47,680
I'll grant you one power
that is second to none!

105
00:05:51,110 --> 00:05:52,540
This is my gamer's intuition talking,

106
00:05:52,540 --> 00:05:55,590
but all of the abilities and equipment
here are totally broken!

107
00:05:55,940 --> 00:05:59,830
If I'm going to a world where magic exists,
I absolutely have to try it out!

108
00:06:00,870 --> 00:06:02,790
Hey, hurry it up.

109
00:06:02,790 --> 00:06:04,950
No matter what you pick, it's all the same.

110
00:06:04,950 --> 00:06:07,510
Nobody's expecting much from
a shut-in game otaku anyway.

111
00:06:07,510 --> 00:06:09,630
I-I'm not an otaku!

112
00:06:09,630 --> 00:06:12,510
And I died after leaving my house,
so I'm not a shut-in, either!

113
00:06:14,760 --> 00:06:17,450
None of that matters. Just hurry it up.

114
00:06:17,450 --> 00:06:20,650
I've still got lots more deceased
humans to guide, you know.

115
00:06:20,650 --> 00:06:21,980
Damn her!

116
00:06:22,380 --> 00:06:26,560
Getting all cocky just because
she's a little bit cute...

117
00:06:31,280 --> 00:06:32,960
"Hurry up and decide," huh?

118
00:06:33,680 --> 00:06:35,410
I'll do just that, then.

119
00:06:35,410 --> 00:06:38,370
Pick one thing to bring to
this parallel world, right?

120
00:06:38,370 --> 00:06:39,630
That's right.

121
00:06:42,590 --> 00:06:43,940
Okay, I pick you.

122
00:06:50,630 --> 00:06:53,660
All right, stand there and
don't leave the magic circle—

123
00:06:54,630 --> 00:06:56,250
What did you just say?

124
00:07:02,950 --> 00:07:04,770
We have heard your request.

125
00:07:04,770 --> 00:07:09,030
I shall take over your job
from here on out, Aqua-sama.

126
00:07:09,030 --> 00:07:09,660
Huh?

127
00:07:10,320 --> 00:07:14,870
Satou Kazuma-san's wish complies with
the regulations and has been accepted.

128
00:07:14,870 --> 00:07:18,380
Hey, what is all this? Wh-What?
You've got to be kidding.

129
00:07:18,380 --> 00:07:20,870
No, no, no! Come on, um...

130
00:07:20,870 --> 00:07:25,350
This is not right! Taking a goddess
with you is against the rules!

131
00:07:25,350 --> 00:07:28,210
It must be illegal! This has to be illegal!

132
00:07:28,210 --> 00:07:30,720
Wait! Wait!

133
00:07:30,990 --> 00:07:33,430
Please have a safe trip, Aqua-sama.

134
00:07:33,430 --> 00:07:35,630
Should you successfully defeat the Devil King,

135
00:07:35,630 --> 00:07:37,220
I will send someone to pick you up.

136
00:07:37,430 --> 00:07:40,230
I may have the ability to
heal since I'm a goddess,

137
00:07:40,230 --> 00:07:42,500
but I have no fighting ability to speak of!

138
00:07:42,500 --> 00:07:45,500
There's no way I can beat the Devil King!

139
00:07:45,500 --> 00:07:48,300
Hey, wait!

140
00:07:49,360 --> 00:07:54,200
How does it feel to get dragged away with
the guy you treated like a total idiot?

141
00:07:56,320 --> 00:07:59,810
You've been designated as the one
thing I'll be bringing along,

142
00:07:59,810 --> 00:08:01,930
so if you're a goddess,
use your godly powers

143
00:08:01,930 --> 00:08:04,080
or whatever to make my
life as easy as possible!

144
00:08:04,080 --> 00:08:05,740
No!

145
00:08:05,740 --> 00:08:08,960
I don't want to go to a parallel
world with a man like this!

146
00:08:13,150 --> 00:08:17,510
Brave hero, I pray that of the
great many prospective heroes,

147
00:08:17,510 --> 00:08:20,710
you will be the one to defeat the Devil King.

148
00:08:20,710 --> 00:08:23,320
If you do so, we shall grant any wish

149
00:08:23,320 --> 00:08:25,940
you desire as a gift from the gods.

150
00:08:25,940 --> 00:08:27,360
Whoa, for real?!

151
00:08:28,190 --> 00:08:29,440
That's my line!

152
00:08:29,440 --> 00:08:31,690
Now, go forth on your journey!

153
00:08:34,780 --> 00:08:37,660
No!

154
00:08:57,390 --> 00:08:58,550
The Town of Beginning Adventurers

155
00:08:58,550 --> 00:08:58,930
The Town of Beginning Adventurers

156
00:08:58,550 --> 00:08:58,930
Axel

157
00:08:58,930 --> 00:08:59,810
The Town of Beginning Adventurers

158
00:08:58,930 --> 00:08:59,810
Axel

159
00:08:59,810 --> 00:08:59,930
The Town of Beginning Adventurers

160
00:08:59,810 --> 00:08:59,930
Axel

161
00:08:59,930 --> 00:09:01,390
The Town of Beginning Adventurers

162
00:08:59,930 --> 00:09:01,390
Axel

163
00:09:03,700 --> 00:09:04,960
It's a parallel world.

164
00:09:05,210 --> 00:09:07,340
Hey, this really is a parallel world!

165
00:09:07,940 --> 00:09:12,440
W-Wait, I'm really going to be using magic

166
00:09:12,440 --> 00:09:15,740
and going on adventures
in this world from now on?

167
00:09:18,370 --> 00:09:22,310
Goodbye, shut-in life! Hello, new world!

168
00:09:22,310 --> 00:09:25,130
I can really start anew in this world!

169
00:09:26,150 --> 00:09:27,630
Hey, shut up.

170
00:09:27,630 --> 00:09:31,380
What am I going to do if everyone
thinks I'm friends with a crazy woman?

171
00:09:31,380 --> 00:09:35,470
More importantly, isn't there something you're
supposed to give me at a time like this?

172
00:09:35,470 --> 00:09:37,790
Look at what I'm wearing. I'm in a tracksuit.

173
00:09:37,790 --> 00:09:41,310
Here I am in a fantasy world,
and all I have is a single tracksuit.

174
00:09:41,310 --> 00:09:43,650
Isn't there a bare minimum of
starter equipment I should—

175
00:09:53,970 --> 00:09:55,990
Wh-What the heck?! Stop! Stop it!

176
00:09:55,990 --> 00:09:58,450
I get it, okay?! I'm sorry!

177
00:09:58,450 --> 00:10:00,940
If you hate it that much,
then you can go home.

178
00:10:00,940 --> 00:10:02,830
I'll work out the rest on my own.

179
00:10:03,030 --> 00:10:04,850
What are you talking about?!

180
00:10:04,850 --> 00:10:06,760
I'm in trouble because I can't go back!

181
00:10:06,760 --> 00:10:08,690
What do I do? Huh? What am I gonna do?

182
00:10:08,690 --> 00:10:11,570
What am I supposed to do from now on?!

183
00:10:12,800 --> 00:10:14,250
Hey, calm down, Goddess.

184
00:10:14,510 --> 00:10:16,230
Times like these call for guilds.

185
00:10:16,770 --> 00:10:21,720
Going to places like that to gather
intel is what you do in RPGs.

186
00:10:21,720 --> 00:10:25,520
Huh? You're supposed to be
some game otaku shut-in.

187
00:10:25,520 --> 00:10:27,270
Why are you so reliable?

188
00:10:27,700 --> 00:10:28,890
All right! Let's go, Goddess.

189
00:10:28,890 --> 00:10:30,200
Hey, wait.

190
00:10:31,330 --> 00:10:33,720
You can call me "Goddess" if you like,

191
00:10:33,720 --> 00:10:36,650
but when you can, call me "Aqua,"
so we don't cause a commotion.

192
00:10:36,650 --> 00:10:37,770
I get it.

193
00:10:38,260 --> 00:10:39,160
If you're a goddess,

194
00:10:39,160 --> 00:10:42,450
wouldn't you know where we can
find an adventurer's guild?

195
00:10:42,450 --> 00:10:44,010
I'm a goddess.

196
00:10:44,010 --> 00:10:47,410
There's no way I'd know about
every little lowly place like that.

197
00:10:49,220 --> 00:10:51,170
This girl's useless...

198
00:10:51,170 --> 00:10:52,210
Thanks for your business.

199
00:10:52,210 --> 00:10:54,340
Thank you. Up we go...

200
00:10:55,470 --> 00:10:55,920
Adventurer's Guild

201
00:10:55,920 --> 00:10:56,170
Adventurer's Guild

202
00:10:56,170 --> 00:10:57,300
Adventurer's Guild

203
